From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Roman Leventov <leventov.ru@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 24 Jul 2026 17:19:25 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 18/28] scheduler: admit durable actions before claim

Prepare scheduled and registered-cron actions while their durable jobs remain Pending. Add a two-way execution-start barrier so V8 owns normal queue, active-permit, and selected-worker capacity, and Node completes application-side preparation, before a fresh exact-state transaction commits Pending to InProgress.

Keep polling the prepared execution while the claim is in flight so a known-lost reservation is never released. Preserve conservative InProgress recovery for ambiguous or post-claim failures, and do not reintroduce the rejected InProgress to Pending ABA retry.

Add bounded admission and claim metrics, focused barrier coverage, patch-train integration notes, rollout guidance, and rejected-alternative analysis.
